\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N=\{1,2,\ldots\}$, and $\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$ denote the integers, rationals, reals and complex numbers. Any other conventions are specified locally.


Let $n\ge1$ and let $f(z)=\prod_{j=1}^n(z-z_j)$ be a monic polynomial of degree $n$, with zeros repeated according to multiplicity. Its filled unit lemniscate is the compact set
\[E_f=\{z\in\mathbb C:|f(z)|\le1\}.
\]
The monic normalization is the one used in the source's Problem 4.7 and its following lemniscate questions.
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
If $E_f$ is connected, is it true that
\[\max_{z\in E_f}|f'(z)|\le\tfrac12n^2?\]
The source's Update 4.8 explains that this historical bound is false and gives the sharp replacement
\[\max_{z\in E_f}|f'(z)|\le 2^{1/n-1}n^2.
\]
The original bound and its corrected sharp version concern the same monic connected-lemniscate class. \href{https://arxiv.org/pdf/1809.07200}{[S2]}

\subsection{Short English statement}
Bound the derivative of a monic polynomial on its connected unit lemniscate. The originally proposed constant is false; the source records the stated sharp correction.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{description}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, \emph{UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems}, record 2304008 (AMR-022-4008). CC BY 4.0. \url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Walter K. Hayman and Edward F. Lingham, \emph{Research Problems in Function Theory}, arXiv:1809.07200, 2018. Lemniscate notation preceding Problem 4.7, Problem 4.7, Problem 4.8 and its complete Update 4.8. \url{https://arxiv.org/pdf/1809.07200}.
\end{description}
